WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.730
- You like acting even more than singing?

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:02.760
I feel like we're opposites.

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:03.770
- We're, we're little bit,

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:04.603
yeah, we're opposites

00:00:04.603 --> 00:00:06.220
and I, I think I kind of knew that

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:07.510
when I was going onto Idol,

00:00:07.510 --> 00:00:10.280
I think I knew that I was gonna
try and go into television

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:11.610
and I wanted to sing,

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:13.130
but I've been really lucky to find shows

00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:13.980
that have
- Yeah.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:14.840
- both the acting and the singing,

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:15.673
like I did Smash

00:00:15.673 --> 00:00:17.630
and now this newest one

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:19.940
with music and I, yeah, I think I,

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:23.070
I like hiding behind the
guise of somebody else.

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:26.310
I mean, I, being, putting an
album out like Katherine McPhee

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:27.143
or Kelly Clarkson,

00:00:27.143 --> 00:00:28.190
- Yeah.
- there's so much,

00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:29.490
there's something so
vulnerable about that,

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:30.323
not that I'm--

00:00:30.323 --> 00:00:32.310
- I have never named an
album Kelly Clarkson.

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:33.143
- Okay.

00:00:33.143 --> 00:00:33.976
- There's a reason.

00:00:33.976 --> 00:00:34.809
- There's a reason maybe.

00:00:34.809 --> 00:00:36.180
- Yeah, it's a lot of pressure.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:37.480
- I made that mistake, the first album.

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:38.530
- Oh, I did not do that.

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:39.475
I was like, can't do it.

00:00:39.475 --> 00:00:41.510
- Yeah, but there's,
there's something, you know,

00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:43.110
it's, you're selling yourself, right.

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:44.360
Like you are the instrument

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:47.120
and so, I don't know, I
think I just really like

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:48.740
standing behind somebody's words

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:50.570
and whether I connect
to those words or not

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:51.710
as a different person

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:53.130
- Yeah.
- and so, yeah, I've always,

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:54.100
I've always liked acting,

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:56.020
but I didn't realize that
it would be the thing

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:57.520
that I really ended up pursuing.

00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:00.130
I was already pursuing it
before I went on Idol, but

00:01:00.130 --> 00:01:01.826
- Yeah.
- I kind of went,

00:01:01.826 --> 00:01:02.659
I spent a lot of,

00:01:02.659 --> 00:01:03.730
a lot of years auditioning for stuff

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:04.650
and not getting them

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:07.240
and making relationships,
so yeah I love it.

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:08.073
- I think you're right.

00:01:08.073 --> 00:01:10.290
I tell people that like
artists on The Voice that too,

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:11.810
that are on my team or
even on other teams,

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:14.620
I'm like don't look at this
as, this is your big thing,

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:15.453
- Right.
- Look at this as like

00:01:15.453 --> 00:01:16.286
the next step
- The next stop.

00:01:16.286 --> 00:01:17.960
because even after I won,

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:20.020
like I was playing like
state fair is nobody,

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:21.020
like, it was hard.

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:21.970
- Oh yeah.
- Like, like it,

00:01:21.970 --> 00:01:23.780
you, you still have to keep working,

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:24.670
like it doesn't just
- Oh yeah.

00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:25.503
- like overnight.

00:01:25.503 --> 00:01:28.020
- Well, 'cause Idol is a, an amazing,

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.770
it's like a camp right
where you're learning stuff,

00:01:29.770 --> 00:01:32.220
but I, I did not know anything
about live performing.

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:33.401
I didn't know how to command a stage,

00:01:33.401 --> 00:01:35.190
I did the same thing, I did state fairs

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:36.170
and there was literally,

00:01:36.170 --> 00:01:38.250
it was, it could have filled 10,000 people

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:39.170
and there were a hundred people there

00:01:39.170 --> 00:01:40.650
and I had to really learn,

00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:41.483
- Yeah.
- you know,

00:01:41.483 --> 00:01:42.316
that helped my acting.

00:01:42.316 --> 00:01:43.149
- To navigate back.

00:01:43.149 --> 00:01:45.040
- To navigate that--
- Humility.

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:46.836
- How's everyone doing out there?

00:01:46.836 --> 00:01:48.132
(clapping)

00:01:48.132 --> 00:01:49.150
(laughing)

00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:51.305
- And I was like, okay, I'm gonna just.

00:01:51.305 --> 00:01:53.956
- Just gonna nail this for all 12 of you.

00:01:53.956 --> 00:01:54.880
- All 12 of you,

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:56.764
but I had several shows like that,

00:01:56.764 --> 00:01:57.597
- Yeah.
- like hundreds of shows

00:01:57.597 --> 00:01:58.464
like that.
- It builds character.

00:01:58.464 --> 00:01:59.550
- It does, it builds character.

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:00.963
- It, yeah.

00:02:00.963 --> 00:02:03.880
- And you learn how to just
kind of push through it and,

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:05.080
and find a way to enjoy it just

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:06.990
for what it is, no matter how
many people are out there.

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:09.240
So it helped both singing
and acting I think.

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:10.570
- I love that.

